 "_about": "Shared by backend/tests/services/test_facility_placement_cases.py and frontend/features/s1/tests/facilityPlacementCases.test.ts. Each case is one document with one or more records. A field is [value, status]; status is rule (read by the rules, not reviewed), ai_only (read only by Claude, nobody accepted it), accepted (Claude read it and a reviewer accepted it), rejected or needs_more_evidence (a reviewer decided against using it). expect.facility has one entry per record: the Setup facility id it is placed on, or null. expect.note has one entry per record: null, or text the plain-sentence note must contain. A field may be a list of readings ([[value, status], ...], in the order read). Optional per case: company (a key with null means no company), decision (the reviewer's own facility choice), type (\"electricity\" for a purchased electricity bill; gas by default). expect.reason, when present, is the recalculation's reason for the unplaced record (a single-record case). The company is the engagement's own (client_name); the name and address rules are #282's (match, ambiguous or none).",
